  "summary": "Security-research / proof-of-concept package: dojo-rn-interview (npm)",
  "details": "The package's preinstall hook runs index.js, which collects system information from the installing machine — hostname, username, home directory, DNS servers, install path, and the full contents of /etc/passwd and /etc/hosts — and POSTs this data over HTTPS to the Burp Collaborator endpoint kqepxa9s4krgw7e7b6f7kufiy943stgi[.]oastify[.]com. The exfiltrated data includes the local /etc/passwd file, exposing system account information. The exfiltration runs automatically on install with no user interaction.",
